  "title": "Gunpowder empires of Asia",
  "summary": "The Ottomans were famous for their gunpowder weapons, including light and heavy cannons, and their janissaries carried arquebuses. The Safavid army's failure to use artillery at the Battle of Chaldiran in 1514 was largely responsible for its defeat by them, and Shah Ismail reacted swiftly by organizing firearms troops. The Mughals have their own records.",
